known_false_positives.description:
Re-exporting `CHAIN_INFO_MAX_RECEIVED_LOG_ENTRIES` from `chain_worker::mod` makes it part of the `chain_worker` module API surface and encourages cross-module coupling (e.g., `client` now imports it). If this constant is intended as an internal implementation detail of ChainInfo pagination, consider keeping it in `state` and exposing a dedicated helper/API instead, or at least making the re-export `pub(crate)`/documenting stability guarantees (semver) if this is meant to be consumed outside the crate.

```suggestion
    // Consider limiting visibility if not part of the public API:
    // pub(crate) use state::CHAIN_INFO_MAX_RECEIVED_LOG_ENTRIES;
    state::BlockOutcome,
```
